<title>FRANCE: Euro-dollar parity does not arise now-BoF official.</title>
<headline>Euro-dollar parity does not arise now-BoF official.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The question of the exchange rates between the euro and the dollar does not arise at the moment since no-one can predict the level of the dollar at the launch of European monetary union, Bank of France deputy governor Herve Hannoun said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;No-one can predict the rate between the euro and dollar at the end of 1998,&quot; he told a business conference.</p>
<p>The question of the euro-dollar exchange rate therefore &quot;does not arise immediately,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>He repeated that it was important for the euro to be a solid currency.</p>
<p>&quot;This is naturally a factor which allows one to think that the euro zone will be a zone with relatively low interest rates,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
